  "description": "The Rhino – AT7 is engineered for riders who want raw torque, real suspension, and zero compromises. This isn’t a toy e-bike — it’s a compact beast built to charge hard through streets, dirt, and everything in between.\nPowered by a 60V 1200W high-speed brushless motor pushing 120 N·m of torque, the Rhino – AT7 delivers instant pull and a limited speed of up to 20 MPH. From launches to hill climbs, it hits with authority. The aluminum frame paired with KKE air rear suspension and a 20” oil-suspension front fork keeps the ride planted and controlled, soaking up impacts whether you’re bombing pavement or cutting through rough terrain. Fat 20x4.0 Vee Huntsman tires on wide 80mm double-wall rims give you unmatched grip, stability, and confidence at speed.\nA Samsung 60V 20Ah battery provides reliable power with a fast 5–6 hour charge time, while the sine-wave smart controller delivers smooth, responsive throttle control. Stopping power comes from hydraulic disc brakes with a 203mm rotor, ensuring precise braking when it matters most.",
